# YAML Support Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use
> superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or
> superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.
> Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Add YAML linting to `harper-ls` (and, for free, `harper-cli`)
by extending the existing `harper-comments` tree-sitter masker
pattern, so `#` comments and prose-like scalar values in `.yaml`/`.yml`
files get grammar-checked while structural YAML (keys, identifiers,
enum-like values) is left alone.

**Architecture:** A new `YamlMasker` in `harper-comments` runs two
independent tree-sitter passes over the same parsed YAML tree — one
selecting `comment` nodes (kept unconditionally, same
`spellchecker:ignore`-style suppression as every other language), one
selecting scalar-value nodes (`plain_scalar`, `single_quote_scalar`,
`double_quote_scalar`, `block_scalar`), each scalar filtered through a
small prose heuristic before being kept. Both passes' surviving spans
are combined into one `Mask`, which existing `Mask<M, P>` /
`Unit::new_markdown` plumbing then hands to Harper's regular English
grammar checking, unchanged.

**Tech Stack:** Rust, `tree-sitter` 0.25, new dependency
`tree-sitter-yaml` 0.7.2, existing `harper-core`/`harper-tree-sitter`
masking primitives.

